     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about double the maximum recommended metformin dose. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. Doses this high raise the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the usual max.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **Another dose**, such as a typo for 170 mg or 700 mg.\n\nIf you meant to start therapy, the usual approach is 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, titrated up every 1\u20132 weeks as tolerated.\n\nIf you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
